WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.620
- Hi, I'm Ari and I got a
hundred people at my work

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:06.210
to stop sucking for a week
and it made me think about

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:08.260
how I could get more
people to stop sucking.

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:10.770
This is a story about how
I went my state's capitol,

00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:13.480
Sacramento, to try to
help get Californians to

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:16.193
stop using single use plastic straws.

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:17.983
But wait, why?

00:00:18.966 --> 00:00:20.513
- [Person] Aww man!

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:24.870
- [Ari] 500 million
plastic straws are used

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:28.040
in the U.S. every day many
of those straws end up

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:29.840
in the ocean and can harm sea life.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:32.250
Reports predict that by 2050 there will be

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:34.853
more plastic I the ocean than fish.

00:00:34.964 --> 00:00:37.533
My journey starts with Shelia Morovati.

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:40.110
She's a mom in L.A. who's
instrumental in getting

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:42.670
the city of Malibu to ban straws.

00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:44.620
- We found this many
straws just walking for

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:45.993
five minutes at the beach.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:47.980
So I went to the city and I asked if they

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:50.310
would implement the ban,
and not only did they vote

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:52.770
on it unanimously,
banning all plastic straws

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:54.973
but also plastic cutlery and stirrers.

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:55.900
- That's amazing

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:57.006
- It was awesome.

00:00:57.006 --> 00:00:59.180
- After talking to Shelia I
was so inspired and I wanted

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:01.750
to see how I could get
involved to address the problem

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:03.383
of single use plastic straws.

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:05.230
So I decided to do some research.

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:06.720
I discovered that Ian Calderon,

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:08.620
the California State assembly leader,

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:11.073
had created a bill called
Straws Upon Request.

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:13.667
I called his office to ask if
he would tell me more about it

00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:15.160
and he agreed to meet with me.

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:17.125
- It's a really easy,
simple bill, it just says

00:01:17.125 --> 00:01:20.000
you go into a full service,
dine-in restaurant,

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.770
you want a straw, you can have it,

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:22.970
you just have to request it.

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:24.580
So, straws upon request.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:27.233
We're not banning it, but
we are raising awareness,

00:01:27.410 --> 00:01:30.640
and I think it's gonna cut down
on the prevalence of straws.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:33.140
- How do you think
people can get involved?

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:35.520
- The best type of advocacy is always

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:37.070
to reach out to your elected officials.

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:39.750
So you have assembly member
Laura Friedman, who is amazing

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:40.763
- Okay. Okay, great.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:42.840
- And your State Senator is Kevin De Leon.

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:45.460
It depends on what
you're willing to do, so,

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:47.629
you can go into your
assembly member's office,

00:01:47.629 --> 00:01:48.462
- Mm hmm

00:01:48.462 --> 00:01:49.295
- You can even write your
assembly member a letter,

00:01:49.295 --> 00:01:50.744
or you can call in.
- Okay.

00:01:50.744 --> 00:01:51.577
- That's what you can do locally.

00:01:51.577 --> 00:01:52.410
- Yeah.

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:53.896
- The next thing is you've
got to fly to Sacramento.

00:01:53.896 --> 00:01:56.723
- Oh.

00:01:59.112 --> 00:02:01.073
- I'd love to have you
there, it's really cool.

00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:04.230
- Oh 100%.

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:06.280
- About to get on the plane to Sacramento

00:02:06.354 --> 00:02:07.486
(pilot on intercom)

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:10.120
- I just arrived, I feel
like I'm on Parks and Rec.

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:13.143
So I'm a little nervous
can you give me any advice?

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:15.280
- [Shelia] Go out there, be positive,

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:16.980
and make your case known.

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:18.533
- Thank you so much Shelia.

00:02:18.552 --> 00:02:20.550
We're going to be presenting the bill

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:23.640
at the natural resources
committee, and if it passes,

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:25.840
it will move along to
the California Senate.

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:27.930
She's gonna be a witness
and I'm gonna testify.

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:28.773
Are you nervous?

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:30.790
- I mean, not really, cuz it's something

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:33.345
that needs to be done, so,
it's just, just gotta do it.

00:02:33.345 --> 00:02:34.178
- Yeah?

00:02:34.461 --> 00:02:35.294
- Yeah.

00:02:35.294 --> 00:02:38.290
- Alright welcome everyone, to
start us off is Mr. Calderon

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:40.390
- And the reason why I'm doing this bill,

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:43.550
is because we have an issue
with single use plastics

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:45.750
- I learned about the problem
that plastic pollution

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:48.740
poses to our ocean as a volunteer
teen conservation leader

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:50.330
at the Monterey Bay Aquarium,

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:52.010
and decided to take action for my

00:02:52.010 --> 00:02:53.600
Girl Scout Gold Award project.

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:56.840
I founded Jr. Ocean Guardians,
an organization dedicated

00:02:56.840 --> 00:03:00.000
to educating people about the
problem of plastic pollution

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:02.160
I urge each and every one
of you to vote in favor of

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:03.723
this congressman's legislation.

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:05.320
- Any further witnesses in support

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:07.033
of this bill please come forward.

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:10.920
- Hi, my name is Ari Jackson
and I'm here, to testify

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:13.550
in support of this bill and
also to show that there is

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:15.293
strong public support for it.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:18.210
I'm a video producer at Buzz
Feed and I made a video about

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:20.483
why straws are harmful to our environment.

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:23.340
This video was viewed on
Facebook 20 million times

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:25.673
and it got 194,000 shares.

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:27.950
The top audience for this video

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:31.220
was Californians ages 25 to 34.

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:33.020
The public, is,

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:36.500
very excited about this bill,
and I urge you to protect

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:39.350
the health of our oceans in California.

00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:40.183
Thank you.

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:41.253
- Thank you very much.

00:03:41.253 --> 00:03:42.086
- [Ari] So how do you think it went.

00:03:42.086 --> 00:03:43.242
- It went as expected, and, you know,

00:03:43.242 --> 00:03:44.075
- Yeah

00:03:44.075 --> 00:03:44.908
- I'm feeling confident

00:03:44.908 --> 00:03:45.741
about the overall solution of the bill.

00:03:45.741 --> 00:03:47.450
- Yeah. I was nervous
but I think it went well.

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:48.568
- No, you did a really good job

00:03:48.568 --> 00:03:50.768
- Okay, I stumbled a
little bit, I was like,

00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:51.613
up there I was like oh no!

00:03:51.613 --> 00:03:52.830
- It's totally normal.

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:53.770
I mean cuz it's funny, like,

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:55.812
right when you get up there,
you know exactly what you're

00:03:55.812 --> 00:03:57.620
going to say when you're going, right?

00:03:57.620 --> 00:03:58.453
- Yeah.

00:03:58.453 --> 00:03:59.383
- And then you get
there and it's just like

00:03:59.383 --> 00:04:01.200
- And like in the middle,
yeah I got a little fumble,

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.230
but, you guys all did great.

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:04.320
Yay, thank you!

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:05.153
- Of course.

00:04:05.153 --> 00:04:06.950
- The Straws Upon Request
bill passed through

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:09.230
the assembly floor and
it is currently waiting

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:11.653
to be approved on the
California Senate floor.

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:14.780
If you want to see it pass,
and reach Governor Brown's desk

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:17.453
call your representatives
to tell them you support it.

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:20.030
Curbing single use straw
use is a great start,

00:04:20.030 --> 00:04:21.540
but they are just one facet of

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:23.403
our single use plastic problem.

00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:25.640
I believe one person can
make a difference, and

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:27.860
if you do to please sign our pledge below

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:29.863
to not use plastic straws anymore.

00:04:30.340 --> 00:04:32.540
- You know I still get tweets
all the time talking about

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:35.090
how I suck because I'm
going to put people in jail.

00:04:35.205 --> 00:04:36.990
Even though it's not even in the bill.

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:39.040
The penalty's were not
what I put in the bill,

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:41.782
they were prescribed in my
bill due to the code section.

00:04:41.782 --> 00:04:42.615
- Yeah.

00:04:42.615 --> 00:04:43.448
- But that's okay, because it's part

00:04:43.448 --> 00:04:44.281
of the legislative process.

00:04:44.281 --> 00:04:47.610
I know that, and I know
ultimately, what the end result is,

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:48.863
and it's all worth it.

